{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nX = \\colim_{i \\in \\mathcal{I}} M_i.\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$M_i \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$i \\in \\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0011": "$X \\to M_i$", "MATH_0012": "$X \\to M_i \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\text{id}_X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b6b54e9c5dd5bcea5f0691d5566861a4e4b6b36a05690f58d65bb22bb11ec285", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:100d4dbe9490d202ebb81c91569a9571a72540761fcf1b8505c413210c04fc7c", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a diagram in a category <MATH_0002>.\nAssume the index category <MATH_0003> is filtered. In this case\nthere are three successively stronger notions which pick out an object\n<MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>. The first is just\n<MATH_0006>\nThen <MATH_0007> comes equipped with the coprojections <MATH_0008>.\nA stronger condition would be to require that <MATH_0009> is the colimit and\nthat there exist an <MATH_0010> and a morphism <MATH_0011> such\nthat the composition <MATH_0012> is <MATH_0013>. An even\nstronger condition is the following.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5fb6df1427f101b5d6fefe2bdf132b0f1bcfbc3a2e66625e84dfd81c567889e1", "unit_id": "tag:05PT:paragraph-0001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-ind-category}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{remark-pro-category}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9ea271f07dedf31e23bccfcca7b1a48df03bc4202a6f905d9c5f2c5052e7abe6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7144f29663c1478cd5cd324f00399b655117a099f8ab26bf8816aa4c91ede5d6", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWhich of the two versions is meant will be clear from context. If there is\nany confusion we will distinguish between these by saying that the first\nversion means <MATH_0001> is essentially constant as an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>ind-object<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, and in\nthe second case we will say it is essentially constant as a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>pro-object<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>.\nThis terminology is further explained in\nRemarks <REF_0001> and <REF_0002>.\nIn fact we will often use the terminology ``essentially constant system''\nwhich formally speaking is only defined for systems over directed sets.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9188d5e41bb54672245ffd7baaa4598fc208cbb7fb6aaeeda727b4600830ceba", "unit_id": "tag:05PT:paragraph-0002"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "05PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$(M_i, f_{ii'})$", "MATH_0003": "$M$", "MATH_0004": "$I \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$(M_i, f_{ii'})$", "MATH_0006": "$M$", "MATH_0007": "$I^{opp} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-essentially-constant-system}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:76518778857495ee1fcf9c39a7e81cc39c2f14c850ffd609a7935b14beef0cfc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62c9e793984f90b81b3fd7c14882e4fadd018d4de38c6568145c315fdc8fbdca", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. A directed system\n<MATH_0002> is an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>essentially constant system<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif <MATH_0003> viewed as a functor <MATH_0004>\ndefines an essentially constant diagram. A directed inverse system\n<MATH_0005> is an <TEXTITOPEN_0002>essentially constant inverse system<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if\n<MATH_0006> viewed as a functor <MATH_0007> defines an\nessentially constant inverse diagram.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0e833937401ab106d17539c6c87f20a72665a3893b5b291bf402292812b55d47", "unit_id": "tag:05PV:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05PT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$M : \\mathcal{I} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0003": "$M$", "MATH_0004": "$X = \\colim M_i$", "MATH_0005": "$M$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0008": "$M$", "MATH_0009": "$X = \\lim M_i$", "MATH_0010": "$M$", "MATH_0011": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-essentially-constant-is-limit-colimit}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:05c71a98654f39faad0d20375d67fe7c45526260fda0a2e464a8f413ca33bef7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35853263bee172e0e6a755e27616fbec69286d8faae57253717d89bc7d732203", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a diagram.\nIf <MATH_0002> is filtered and <MATH_0003> is essentially\nconstant as an ind-object, then <MATH_0004> exists and <MATH_0005>\nis essentially constant with value <MATH_0006>.\nIf <MATH_0007> is cofiltered and <MATH_0008> is essentially\nconstant as a pro-object, then <MATH_0009> exists and <MATH_0010> is\nessentially constant with value <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f5fb1d95377fa642c22f35baec9d9449bb00509b32bd16af46997f98bc3c74a", "unit_id": "tag:0G2V:statement"}
