too. Setting <MATH_0009> and starting with <MATH_0010>\nin the colimit, we see that <MATH_0011> is equal to\n<MATH_0012> for some <MATH_0013> large enough. This proves (1) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume (4). Let <MATH_0014> be an object of <MATH_0015>. Setting <MATH_0016>\nwe deduce there exists a unique morphism <MATH_0017> such that\nthere exists a <MATH_0018> and morphisms <MATH_0019> and\n<MATH_0020> in <MATH_0021> such that <MATH_0022>\nis equal to <MATH_0023>. The uniqueness guarantees that we obtain a\ncocone <MATH_0024>. In this way we see that (4) implies (2);\nsome details omitted.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nWe omit the proof that (1) implies the other conditions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:790099d2c7a5c3bb75032dac4fbc83303e5f34c27adc7769b1252c939a555ded", "unit_id": "tag:05PY:proof"}
